# DESK20: assign a function key in the Install-Application dialog and see it
# in Desktop configuration. C:\CMDLINE.NCP is selected (which enables the menu
# entry), the document type `TXT` is typed into APDOCTYP, `7` into the new
# APFUNKEY field (desk_rsc.h:119), Install is pressed, and Options -> Desktop
# configuration then shows `F7` + the path in the Function keys panel.
#   C:\ window CMDLINE.NCP (347,145)                                [probe 1]
#   Options: `Install application...` (280,43), `Desktop conf...` (280,123)
#   ADINSAPP: APDOCTYP (368,192), APFUNKEY (360,224), Install (209,350) [probe 4]
#   scancodes: T=14 X=2d 7=08 (make), +0x80 = break
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1500 key 38
1550 key 2e
1600 key ae
1650 key b8
2800 mark B_WIN
3100 move 347 145
3400 down
3403 up
3800 parkbr
4600 mark C_SEL
4900 move 196 240
5300 move 196 9
5900 mark D_MENU
6100 move 280 43
6500 down
6503 up
7100 parkbr
8000 mark E_INSAPP
8200 key 14
8240 key 94
8300 key 2d
8340 key ad
8400 key 14
8440 key 94
9000 mark F_DOCTYPE
9200 move 360 224
9600 down
9603 up
10200 key 08
10240 key 88
10800 parkbr
11600 mark G_FUNKEY
11800 move 209 350
12200 down
12203 up
12800 parkbr
13700 mark H_INSTALLED
14000 move 196 240
14400 move 196 9
15000 mark I_MENU2
15200 move 280 123
15600 down
15603 up
16200 parkbr
17100 mark J_CONF
18600 pause
